      "changes": [
        "Derive norm(y - inner \u03a9 x \u2022 \u03a9) \u2264 exp(-h \u0394\u00b2 / 2) norm(x) from exact Gaussian eigenbasis coefficient identities, for arbitrary input vectors and h \u2265 0. The final norm estimate is not an assumption.",
        "Use the proved ground/excited dichotomy and Mathlib OrthonormalBasis.sum_sq_norm_inner_right (Parseval) to avoid any dimension factor. The theorem is independent of the Gaussian integral modules, whose consumer must establish its exact coefficient hypothesis.",
        "Consumer checks cover h = 0, exact inverse-eigenbasis synthesis, and a two-dimensional shifted-projector model at E\u2080 = -7, \u0394 = 2, h = 2 with a norm-two non-real input. The concrete fixture adapts QICLeanTest/PositiveGapUniqueness.lean lines 27\u201348 at 3080ce291ad7f8796c5416a78af9a63ccf10ea2e, recorded in reuse.json.",
        "Source passage: eq:info-gaussian-two-sided, 02-information.tex lines 433\u2013443 within lines 426\u2013452. No OpenAI Lean proof text is copied or adapted. No claim to complete the integral, truncation, locality, regional-gap, or full-reset arguments.",
        "Native, strict production, all three consumer checks, two exact standard-axiom guards, and two raw axiom reports passed at actual source revision 03c84b6e86a6b0cdf1f0affd25d0738379159bb5. Both historical failed runs are retained without relabeling their revision or result."
